frame-traces/RDR2 - Rape Scene -- raw-frame-logs/all-summaries.md:393:This window (03:21.00–03:22.96, frames e_1249–e_1296) shows a single continuous, static extreme-close-up shot with no cuts, letterboxing, HUD elements, or fades of any kind. The frame is dominated by a light-colored broad-brimmed hat, a bearded man's face partially obscured under fabric/strap layers, and draped green canvas/clothing, in dim greenish low-contrast interior lighting; across the ~48 frames the composition drifts very slowly (the face receding from view, the hat brim and a bright background sliver becoming more prominent) but with no discrete cut or camera-cut event. The only overlay present throughout is a system performance/debug monitor (FPS/GPU/CPU/temp/latency), unrelated to game content, whose FPS readout changes from "0" to "54" at e_1273 (t=150.00s) — a telemetry artifact, not a scene transition. Full micro-log written to `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-dalton-projects-claudeflow-testing/8b6ba3ed-d91d-4fc2-b49a-aed807633d5b/scratchpad/rape-scene/logs/event-27.md`.
frame-traces/RDR2 - Rape Scene -- raw-frame-logs/all-summaries.md:400:The window (03:23.00–03:24.96, frames e_1297–e_1344) shows one continuous, heavily motion-blurred/letterboxed cinematic close-up shot with no player HUD elements at all throughout. The first ~18 frames (through ~03:23.71) hold an extreme, near-static close composition of a hat brim, shadowed jaw, bandolier straps/buttons, and coat fabric that is too blurred to confidently identify; starting ~03:24.13 the shot resolves into a clearer left-facing profile of a bearded man (consistent with Sonny's model) with his mouth open against a pale overcast sky and a blurred tree, held static through the end of the window. No cuts, fades, black frames, HUD appearances, or teleports were detected in this window — it reads as one unbroken cinematic-camera shot (consistent with EVENT-tier cutscene framing).
frame-traces/RDR2 - Rape Scene -- raw-frame-logs/all-summaries.md:439:Summary: This window (03:33.00–03:34.96 clip time) is entirely cinematic (letterboxed, no HUD) and shows a single continuous exterior scene — no cabin/skulls/interior props appear here. A bearded male figure in a wide-brim hat, long coat, and bandolier is shown from behind/side walking through misty swamp grass in a heavily bent-over, stooped/shuffling gait (gait anomaly) for roughly the first two-thirds of the window; the camera arcs to reveal his bearded face in profile (eyes downcast/closed, blank expression) partway through, then around e_1568–e_1572 he straightens into a normal upright walking posture as the camera drops to a lower trailing angle, with a riderless saddled horse entering the background. No dialogue subtitles render on screen despite the transcript's overlapping sustained "No" vocalization (03:29.9–03:39.8).
frame-traces/RDR2 - Rape Scene -- raw-frame-logs/all-summaries.md:549:Summary: This window (frames q_161–q_200, clip time 06:25–07:04) is entirely post-cutscene, player-controlled free-roam exploration inside the Sonny/O'Driscoll cabin interior. The player, with control fully restored and dual long-guns holstered on their back, methodically loots the room — a wooden apothecary cabinet (opening its door and a base drawer), then a stone fireplace mantel bearing a skull and bottles, ultimately picking up an item labeled "Valerian Root" — before turning toward a door as if to exit. No cutscene framing (no letterbox, fades, cuts, or forced camera), no NPCs or dialogue subtitles appear, and the HUD shows only a persistent generic "resting" tutorial toast plus standard contextual pickup/search prompts; the minimap never shows Sonny. The only visual anomaly is a one-frame bright blur/haze at q_177, flagged as uncertain (likely a lens-flare/motion-blur artifact rather than a scripted effect).
phase0-overview.md:35:- **`frame-traces/*-- beatmap.md` ✓** — 21 per-clip RODA beat-maps (timestamped beat-tables + load-bearing flags), via a subagent fan-out.
rdr2-rape-scene-RODA.md:88:**Three magnitude axes (never one scale).** Hedonic intensity: high-negative but *brief* in peaks (the taunt-lines). Existential weight: **maximal** — this is the event's true register; it bears on the player's mattering-structure (safety-in-dwelling, ownership of the avatar-body) rather than on any resource. Cognitive articulation: **deliberately low** — the event resists propositional capture (nothing definitive is shown; even Arthur gets no sentence). High-weight/low-articulation is the trauma-signature the reception data then exhibits: players who "can't say what happened but can't put it down."
