rdr2-element-matrix.md:6:> **⚠ Frame-verification (2026-06-27, see `frame-read-verification.md`).** A targeted visual pass **confirmed** several rows (the inflicted-*bia* hogtie chain [8]; the jointly-sourced collective acts — raid [11], jailbreak [15]; the witness/wanted legal-consequence overlay [13]) and the **scripted** bar-fight trigger [10]. **The HONOR rows — author-confirmed:** honor is **inert** on the choke/spare fork (only the bell) AND on the bar-fight brawl (no change), but **active** on legible pro-social/heroic acts (+honor for camp chores [6]; +10 for defending the weak [7]) — selective along a **public-pro-social vs intimate-ambiguous / ordinary-violence** axis (so any "active on the bar-fight" cell should read *inert*). Distinguish the *moral* honor meter from the *legal* **WANTED / witness system** (bounties; the witness THREATEN/BEAT mechanic; the red search-zone), the visibly-active consequence overlay. Corrections: the bar-fight intervener is a townsman (not Trelawney); the bear/drunk/gambling beats are not at the cited timestamps.
rdr2-element-matrix.md:57:| **Animals-as-quarry** (deer, bear, legendary animal) [4, 9] | A2 — the quarry as determinate charged image fused with the kill-orekton; A4 the kill | Lud + Spa + Aff | Scene/Purpose (provision; legitimate violence) | nature (its fear/charge = co-agent's *orexis*); — | the predatory *technē* | the **charging bear** is the corpus's purest specimen of embodiment-as-flinch (R2 via phantasia, no HMD); "easier when they ain't shooting back" self-marks the low-flinch end |
